riority=\"49\" Name=\"List Table 4 Accent 4\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"50\" Name=\"List Table 5 Dark Accent 4\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"51\"\n   Name=\"List Table 6 Colorful Accent 4\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"52\"\n   Name=\"List Table 7 Colorful Accent 4\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"46\"\n   Name=\"List Table 1 Light Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"47\" Name=\"List Table 2 Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"48\" Name=\"List Table 3 Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"49\" Name=\"List Table 4 Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"50\" Name=\"List Table 5 Dark Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"51\"\n   Name=\"List Table 6 Colorful Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"52\"\n   Name=\"List Table 7 Colorful Accent 5\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"46\"\n   Name=\"List Table 1 Light Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"47\" Name=\"List Table 2 Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"48\" Name=\"List Table 3 Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"49\" Name=\"List Table 4 Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"50\" Name=\"List Table 5 Dark Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"51\"\n   Name=\"List Table 6 Colorful Accent 6\"/>\n  <w:LsdException Locked=\"false\" Priority=\"52\"\n   Name=\"List Table 7 Colorful Accent 6\"/>\n </w:LatentStyles>\n</xml><![endif]--><!--[if gte mso 10]>\n<style>\n /* Style Definitions */\n table.MsoNormalTable\n\t{mso-style-name:\"Обычная таблица\";\n\tmso-tstyle-rowband-size:0;\n\tmso-tstyle-colband-size:0;\n\tmso-style-noshow:yes;\n\tmso-style-priority:99;\n\tmso-style-parent:\"\";\n\tmso-padding-alt:0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\n\tmso-para-margin:0cm;\n\tmso-para-margin-bottom:.0001pt;\n\tmso-pagination:widow-orphan;\n\tfont-size:10.0pt;\n\tfont-family:\"Times New Roman\",serif;\n\tmso-bidi-language:BO;}\n</style>\n<![endif]-->\n\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"hl\">…и учитель Видьякокила, сведущий в философской системе Нагарджуны, а также…</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Нагарджуна башкының ёзу-чаңчылында төлептиг Ригпа Куджуктуң\nсуртаалдары;</p>",
      "confirmed": false,
      "note": "<h2 class=\"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-1v5brwj\" style=\"box-sizing: inherit; margin: 0px 0px 4px; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.5; font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.1429rem; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(250, 250, 250); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">Analysis and Introduction</h2><p class=\"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-18e819t\" style=\"box-sizing: inherit; margin: 0px 0px 16px; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 18.2864px; line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); word-break: break-word; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(250, 250, 250); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">The phrase <em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">klu sgrub kyi lugs la mkhas pa'i rigs pa'i khu byug</em> (often appearing with the variant spelling <em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">rig pa'i khu byug</em>) refers to the Indian master Vidyākokila the Elder (or Younger), known in Tibetan as Rigpa'i Khujuk (རིག་པའི་ཁུ་བྱུག / རིགས་པའི་ཁུ་བྱུག, literally \"Cuckoo of Reasoning\" or \"Cuckoo of Knowledge\"). In Tibetan historiographical and Lamrim (Stages of the Path) literature—most notably in treatises tracing the lineages of the <em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">Bodhicaryāvatāra</em> and the <em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">Prajñāpāramitā</em> instructions through Atiśa Dīpaṃkaraśrījñāna—Vidyākokila represents the pivotal lineage holder of the Profound View (<em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">zab mo lta ba'i brgyud pa</em>) stemming from Nāgārjuna and Candrakīrti.</p><p class=\"MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body1 mui-18e819t\" style=\"box-sizing: inherit; margin: 0px 0px 16px; font-family: &quot;Noto Sans&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 18.2864px; line-height: 1.5; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); word-break: break-word; font-style: normal; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; letter-spacing: normal; orphans: 2; text-align: start; text-indent: 0px; text-transform: none; widows: 2; word-spacing: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; white-space: normal; background-color: rgb(250, 250, 250); text-decoration-thickness: initial; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;\">Within the transmission narratives found in texts such as the Lamrim instructional literature, the third distinctive greatness (<em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">khyad chos gsum pa</em>) of the Kadampa/Lamrim teaching is frequently highlighted: its synthesis of the two primary Indian Mahāyāna lineages. The lineage of the Vast Conduct (<em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">rgya chen spyod pa'i brgyud pa</em>) of Asaṅga and Vasubandhu was received by Atiśa from Guru Suvarṇadvīpi Dharmakīrti (Bla ma Gser gling pa), while the lineage of the Profound View (<em style=\"box-sizing: inherit;\">zab mo lta ba'i brgyud pa</em>) of Nāgārjuna and Candrakīrti was transmitted via the master Vidyākokila. Thus, this phrase designates Vidyākokila as the paragon exponent of Nāgārjuna's Madhyamaka system.</p>",
      "bookmarked": false
    },
    {
      "source": "ཐོགས་མེད་ཀྱི་ལུགས་ལ་མཁས་པའི་གསེར་གླིང་པའི་གདམས་པས་བརྒྱན་པ་ཡིན་པས་འདི་ལྟ་བུ་ལ་ཉན་བསམ་སྒོམ་གསུམ་བྱེད་དུ་ཡོད་པ་ནི་བདག་སྐལ་བ་བཟང་ལ།",
